    These batch files present themselves as "Atlas/ReviOS Tool" in their
    own banners and are named after the AtlasOS and ReviOS projects
    (section 3). Their provenance cannot be determined from the files
    themselves: they carry no copyright notice, no author attribution and
    no license header, so it is not recorded here — because it is not known
    — whether they are original to WinEase, adapted, or copied. They are
    shipped in the release package as post-install tools. Anyone
    redistributing WinEase should verify the origin and license of these
    files first; this notice flags the gap instead of papering over it.

5. oscdimg.exe (bundled binary, repository root)

    oscdimg.exe is a tool of the Microsoft Windows Assessment and
    Deployment Kit (Windows ADK); it is a Microsoft binary, not a WinEase
    work, and Microsoft's terms for the ADK apply to it. The bundled copy
    is version 2.56. WinEase does not trust the file by its presence: at
    build time Test-OscdimgIntegrity (lib/WinEaseSystem.ps1) accepts an
    oscdimg binary only when its Authenticode signature is valid and
    issued by Microsoft, or when its SHA-256 matches a pinned known hash.
